- Similar Artists.
- New Releases.
- Popular in Your Country.
- Trending in Africa.
- Discover New Artists.
- Your Frequently Played Music.
- Recently Played.
10.3 Recommendation ranking
Use a configurable ranking model.

Possible factors:
- User preference match.
- Artist-follow relevance.
- Similarity to liked music.
- Listening behavior.
- Freshness.
- Quality and moderation status.
- Geographic relevance.
- Diversity.
- Repetition penalty.
Do not use unverified plays as the sole popularity signal.

Do not make paid promotion indistinguishable from organic recommendations. Clearly label sponsored placements.
10.4 Recommendation feedback
Listeners can select:
- More like this.
- Less like this.
- Hide this track.
- Don't recommend this artist.
- Not interested in this genre.
- Reset recommendations.
10.5 Cold-start behavior
For new users with no listening history:
- Use optional onboarding preferences.
- Use country and language preferences when supplied.
- Show legitimate trending and new-release content.
- Introduce a diverse selection of African artists.
For new artists:
- Give eligible new releases a discovery opportunity.
- Avoid a system where only established artists receive impressions.
10.6 Future advanced recommendations
After reliable listening data exists:
- Similarity models.
- Collaborative filtering.
- Audio-feature similarity where technically and legally appropriate.
- Personalized ranking.
- Cross-country discovery.
- Context-aware recommendations.
Do not introduce expensive AI infrastructure before reliable foundational data exists.

