17. Track and artist monetization
Music monetization must integrate with the PAYTUNE financial system.

Possible models:
- Free music.
- Paid individual tracks.
- Paid albums.
- Artist tips and gifts.
- Artist memberships.
- Sponsored placements.
- Eligible advertising where policy permits.
- Other approved commercial agreements.
Important:

The existing PAYTUNE master specification describes a 5% VAT deduction and a 70/30 artist/platform split for its video-purchase model. That policy must not automatically be assumed to govern every music product.

Before implementing music sales, Master Owner must approve the applicable:
- Artist royalty agreement.
- Platform fee.
- Tax handling.
- Payment provider fee handling.
- Rights-holder split.
- Refund rules.
- Currency handling.
- Payout conditions.
Music rights may involve multiple contributors. The platform must support approved ownership and revenue-sharing agreements before enabling royalty distributions for collaborative recordings.

Never calculate final earnings in the browser.

