19.14 Migration requirements
Every migration must:
- Be versioned.
- Be additive where possible.
- Include foreign keys.
- Include unique constraints.
- Include indexes.
- Include appropriate check constraints.
- Include rollback or documented recovery procedures.
- Be tested against the actual database schema.
- Avoid deleting existing PAYTUNE data.
- Avoid creating fake production records.
- Be safe to rerun only where the migration framework explicitly supports that behavior.
Use UTC timestamps and stable ISO country/language codes.

Do not assume the existing users.id or artist_profiles.id type without inspecting the actual database.

