31. Existing specification decisions requiring reconciliation
The available PAYTUNE master specification describes an earlier video-first implementation. Before Music development, the engineering team must reconcile these details:
1. Its earlier UI specification says dark mode by default; the current Music requirement is white/light mode by default.
2. Its earlier storage design includes a public audio bucket; protected and paid audio requires a more secure access model.
3. Its earlier follows table must be inspected before adding a new artist-follow relationship.
4. Its existing videos table must be inspected to determine how artist ownership and video publication work.
5. Its existing payment split applies to the specified video model; Music royalties require an explicitly approved policy.
6. Its existing artist approval and copyright review workflow must be reused or extended for music.
7. The actual repository and migrations must be inspected before finalizing column types, file names or migration execution.
Implementation honesty: The available project material contains the master specification, not a verified complete current source-code repository. This PRD therefore defines the target system; it does not claim that its APIs, migrations or features already exist.
32. Final product standard
PAYTUNE Music should be judged by the quality of its relationships and the reliability of its operations, not simply by the number of screens it contains.

A listener must be able to discover a track, follow its artist, return to that artist's page, play another track, watch the related video, save an album and see all those actions reflected consistently throughout the platform.

An artist must be able to manage their music and video identity from one channel and understand their real audience.

The Master Owner must be able to understand platform-wide music activity, enforce policies and audit important operations.

Final principle: One user system. One artist identity. One consistent relationship system. One trusted music catalog. One reliable playback and analytics system.

This is the foundation for a powerful, scalable Pan-African PAYTUNE Music platform.




Important implementation note
This PRD is ready to guide development, but the actual code implementation must begin with a schema and repository audit. I would not run the proposed migrations blindly against the current database: existing PAYTUNE IDs, foreign keys, RLS policies and storage permissions must be checked first.

The first engineering deliverable should be the Music Foundation: verified schema map, additive SQL migrations, RLS policies, artist-follow integration and automated relationship tests. That prevents us from building attractive pages on top of broken relationships.










  






